WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.420
Jim Henson's Muppet Adventure, Chaos at the Carnival, Jump, Leap, Hop, and Charge into Action.

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:32.560
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:33.600
I'm Mike.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:36.240
I'm Sean. And I'm Joe.

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:39.960
Miss Piggy has been pig-napped.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:45.760
Oh, no. For some reason, it just feels like really dirty.

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:50.300
Pig-napped. I actually, I wouldn't have thought pig-napped sounded dirty.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.680
I thought it was like too playful to be taken seriously.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:54.540
Like, oh, all right, she's been pig-napped.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:55.960
Yep. Great.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:57.840
She'll be back next episode.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.520
Like, what's going on? Do you get man-napped?

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:04.060
Is anybody going to care if she gets kidnapped too?

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:08.080
Like, I hate to be that guy, but like, I'm low on Miss Piggy as a Muppet.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:09.640
Yeah. Isn't she kind of abusive?

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:12.360
Absolutely. Is she not canceled yet?

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:19.260
Even if she's, you know, kind of mean, like, that doesn't mean like nobody should care if she's been pig-napped.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:21.060
I mean, I don't know.

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:24.220
I would be worried if you guys got pig-napped.

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:25.400
Aw. And we're mean.

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:27.720
But I would be man-napped, right, to your point earlier?

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:29.060
You would be man-napped, yes.

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:31.520
Yeah. Okay. And do you just become Sean-napped?

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:33.960
Well, I don't know.

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:39.980
I don't know. Like, she's being pig-napped because she's a pig, not because her name is Miss Piggy, right?

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:41.620
Oh, yeah. That's what I meant.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.480
I wasn't really sure where you were going with that.

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:44.480
Yeah. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:45.360
I'm just saying, you're so-

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:46.900
Because I'm not a man. Yeah.

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:49.800
Oh, yeah. Well, are you a man or are you a Muppet?

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:52.820
I don't know.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:54.700
Maybe you're a Muppet of a man.

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:56.120
Oh, I get it.

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:57.000
I didn't see that.

00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:59.460
Oh, okay. Yeah, you're a very manly Muppet.

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:02.640
Are you referencing the musical thing?

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:04.320
Yeah, from the movie.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:06.700
Yeah. Is it the most recent movie?

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:08.460
I don't know. Is that for getting Sarah Marshall?

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:11.720
I can keep track of Muppet stuff. Yes, it is.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:13.800
Okay. Just checking.

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:16.860
Did you guys hear about the kidnapping?

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:19.440
Yeah, I was going to see if you heard about the kidnapping at that school.

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:21.720
That sounds terrible and real.

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:23.080
He woke up. It's okay.

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:26.980
Oh, God damn it.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:28.880
Wow. This will be my last episode, everybody.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:32.840
I was wondering if we were just turning into a breaking news podcast.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:37.820
Because I was like- This is now current events slash knock knock jokes.

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:41.600
Miss Piggy, pignapped, been covered.

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:42.940
Dr. Grump.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:45.060
Anybody know if he's like a real-

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.040
No, I have no idea. He's the one who did the pignapping.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:48.300
Is he from the Muppets?

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:50.100
I assumed he was.

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:51.520
Have we not heard of him?

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:53.260
Did we check the Muppet Wiki?

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:58.400
The Muppet Wiki would know.

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:03.460
So I feel like I owe it to everybody to just do a quick, does he exist?

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:05.700
And it seems like-

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:08.080
Yeah, this podcast would be better if we did a little research.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:09.780
A little research would be great.

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:11.900
It seems like there might be a Dr.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.760
Grumpy. I think that's probably it, right?

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:18.100
Yeah, maybe they just couldn't get enough characters on screen.

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:19.200
No, there is no Dr.

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:22.000
Grump in the Muppets.

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:25.700
There is a Grump, but he doesn't look anything like this guy.

00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:26.800
Well, maybe he's a Grump.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:28.940
Maybe he's just like a doctor for this game.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:30.900
Do you guys ever watch the show?

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:32.320
I love the show.

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:33.280
Don't get me wrong.

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:38.560
But I feel like Grump, it seems like he was like a weird one-off thing in the 60s.

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:42.960
And it would not be referenced in this rather childish Muppets.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:48.920
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah. I wasn't trying to insult you, because I have never really watched the show.

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:59.660
And I was just checking to see if maybe you guys had a bit more historical experience with this franchise.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:07.160
I think when I was a kid, I would catch an episode here and there or something, but I never really watched it.

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:09.640
I was more of a Muppet Babies guy as a little kid.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.040
Yeah, I remember Muppet Babies.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:14.920
I don't remember anything about it.

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:19.080
I just remember that I did watch it at least a few times when I was a kid, but never Muppets.

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:21.660
Muppet Babies is a very cozy show.

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:24.100
That's why you don't remember anything, because you didn't have to.

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:26.180
It was just like you just watched it and you felt good.

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:27.800
Oh, okay. Yeah.

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:39.240
Now, the Muppet show is interesting because it was trying to be a variety sketch show as if it was live and being put together.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:49.880
Like, oh, we're the Muppets and we're trying to make this show, but it's also all obviously scripted and filmed in advance and not live, but it's put on under that guise.

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:54.200
And I think that's a pretty unique hook about the show.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:56.220
So, I dig it.

00:04:56.540 --> 00:05:00.800
And I feel like the main hook of every episode was the guest stars.

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:03.400
There were a lot of guest stars across many different seasons.

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:07.660
And I think even off the show, we were talking about some of the guest stars who showed up.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:10.400
And they got some, like, really big names at the time.

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:17.320
So, I feel like while we know of the Muppets now, they were never hotter than they were in the 70s.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:20.420
Like, that was peak Muppet time for everybody.

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:23.960
And the Muppets have only lost value over time.

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:26.600
I thought they were having a little bit of a resurgence.

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:29.800
They were having that resurgence with the movie, which did do well.

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:35.660
But then they got that show, I believe, on NBC, which was also just called, like, The Muppets.

00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:41.460
And it was, like, same idea of, like, now you're going to watch how they put together this live show and everything.

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:46.900
And it was trying to be a little bit of SNL, a little bit of 30 Rock and all that.

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:48.080
A little bit of jackass.

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:51.040
Sure. But it was none of that, really.

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:55.520
And while I thought it was, like, an okay show, I didn't hate it by any means, it was canceled pretty quickly.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:59.140
Damn. So, people were not, like, coming back for The Muppets.

00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:02.220
Did they have any, like, contemporary, like, co-hosts?

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:04.880
Or was it, like, a single-camera sitcom thing?

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:09.080
It was a single-camera sitcom-style thing.

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:10.100
But there were still guests.

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:13.280
Oh, okay. So, like, Billie Eilish?

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:15.420
It wasn't that recent.

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:17.680
Oh, okay. That's too bad.

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:25.700
They still have enough, you know, they're still big enough that Disney will bank on them for Disney World.

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:31.660
You know, they're making, like, aren't they making, like, a ride and, like, a section of Disney World that's going to be Muppet-themed?

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:34.480
I don't doubt that the Muppets can sell.

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:40.700
Like, I'm sure there are toys and there's plenty of, I feel like just the appetite.

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:47.480
The appetite for the Muppets as a TV show or a media thing is less than as a brand.

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:49.520
Sure. It's kind of crazy, though.

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:59.100
Like, I would have thought that maybe, like, oh, they've had one there and it doesn't, like, the numbers just don't work out to replace it.

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:01.080
Like, it's doing fine as it is.

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:05.160
But, like, to think that they're actually putting resources into making it.

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:10.100
Yeah. I mean, I don't quote me on the fact that there's going to be a whole section.

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:12.620
I think there might be, like, an area that's going to be like a Muppet area.

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:18.860
I'm not sure, but I'm positive they are changing Rockin' Roller Coaster, the Aerosmith roller coaster, into a Muppet roller coaster.

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:20.220
But that sounds fun.

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:22.520
I never knew what Aerosmith was doing at Disney World anyway.

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:31.000
Yeah. It just, that just seems like, you know, as someone who's been to Disney World twice in my life, like, many years apart, that's, like, one that I've always heard of.

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:34.380
You know, it just seems like I knew what Rockin' Roller Coaster was before I went.

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:35.360
I didn't know until this moment.

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:37.380
It's weird that they're getting rid of that for a Muppet thing.

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:47.240
I didn't, I feel like, I know that, like, you know, there's all the Disney princesses and Steven Tyler's among them, but, like, I just didn't think that that was ever a thing.

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:48.920
Who is your favorite Muppet?

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:52.680
Big Bird. Well, does it have to be, yeah, can it be from Sesame Street?

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:54.140
They are Muppets.

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:58.200
I'm not going to, I'm not here to fight on the definition of a Muppet.

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:03.240
Because as a kid, I was obsessed with Oscar the Grouch.

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:07.140
You, you don't strike me as a big fan of Oscar the Grouch.

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:08.820
Do you want to explain this a little bit?

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:11.760
Yeah, I'm a very positive person, but, uh, I don't know, maybe that's why.

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:14.700
Maybe opposites attract, and I just thought Oscar the Grouch was so cool.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:21.700
See, I'm just disappointed that, like, I thought I was making a really bad joke about how I didn't know anything about the Muppets,

00:08:21.780 --> 00:08:28.000
but now you're telling me that they are actually the same, like, kind of moral subject?

00:08:28.260 --> 00:08:33.420
Like, okay. Yeah, technically, like, everything from Fraggle Rock counts as a Muppet.

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:35.860
Yeah. I've never seen Fraggle Rock.

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:36.680
I mean, think Kermit the Frog.

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:41.660
He's like a Sesame Street, he's like the linchpin that holds Sesame Street and the Muppets together.

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:44.580
Well, I thought Jim Henson would have been, but okay.

00:08:44.980 --> 00:08:48.200
Yeah, he's the one with their hand, like, up his ass, right?

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:50.020
That's kind of how it works.

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:55.820
Kermit and Jim Henson were partners on the Muppets.

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:58.320
Yeah, I heard they worked together pretty closely.

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:05.880
And, Mike, since you seem the most versed in the Muppets, can I ask you something about this back of the box?

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:09.120
Yeah. First of all, can you read it again, the back of the box?

00:09:10.220 --> 00:09:12.160
Just the part I read on the show?

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:13.140
Yeah, after the...

00:09:13.140 --> 00:09:17.540
Yeah. Jump, leap, hop, and charge into action.

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:19.620
Okay, so now are those all...

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:23.160
First of all, jump, leap, hop, all synonymous, really.

00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:25.140
I think they're all things Kermit does.

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:27.740
They're all things Kermit does, but it's not anything...

00:09:27.740 --> 00:09:30.260
You don't do any of those things in this game.

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:32.160
Well, you do if you're good.

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:34.780
You do them if you're really good.

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:36.780
Yeah. Oh, you don't know?

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:38.680
I don't know.

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:41.660
All right, well, this is actually a good setup to finally talk about...

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:44.000
It's a good setup to talk about the actual game because...

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:51.440
So, the game is basically a compilation of four minigames that are disguised under this carnival theme.

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:53.800
But you have to...

00:09:54.260 --> 00:10:03.360
You have four carnival rides that star Kermit, Fozzie, Animal, and Gonzo on a sort of a rescue of Miss Piggy.

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:12.680
They have to play the stage long enough, clear a certain amount in order to clear the stage and get the thing that will progress to the end.

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:18.500
And basically, once you do those four carnival rides, the finale is with Kermit in this sort of...

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:20.380
Like, I don't want to...

00:10:20.380 --> 00:10:21.800
Platformers being nice to it.

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:26.520
But, like, yeah, that would be where the leaping and the hopping into action comes into play.

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:34.020
I would just like to make an argument against the idea of these being minigames because they do take a very long time.

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:36.500
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah. Sorry, these are long games.

00:10:36.760 --> 00:10:38.420
Yes, long games.

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:41.040
But long games with the substance of a minigame.

00:10:41.580 --> 00:10:48.640
Absolutely. And then I would also like to argue that there's any characters in this game aside from Kermit because...

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:52.660
Like, Kermit's the only one that has any actual, like, recognizable...

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:54.600
Of the characters that you play.

00:10:54.600 --> 00:11:00.440
Okay. I thought I distinctly recognized Animal as the one, I think, in the car one.

00:11:00.520 --> 00:11:04.360
Yes, yeah. He kind of looks like Elmo if you're not trying, but...

00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:06.900
Yeah. Fozzie, that's clearly him in the maze.

00:11:07.780 --> 00:11:09.160
Okay, you're right.

00:11:09.300 --> 00:11:11.140
The maze and the...

00:11:13.140 --> 00:11:21.020
Which isn't even like a carnival ride going down a river in an inner tube, but...

00:11:21.020 --> 00:11:23.340
Yeah, it's like a lazy river at a water park.

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:25.740
Okay, sure. Not a carnival.

00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:29.840
And you don't go to space at a carnival either, but it's like, that's neither here nor there.

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:38.160
What I'm saying is that they could have done a better job using the sprites to signify that these are the characters from the show.

00:11:39.560 --> 00:11:41.660
I mean, that should have been priority number one, right?

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:47.560
Priority number one, it seems like their biggest thing was just like, hey, how do we get the Muppets in a video game?

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:52.660
Because they're not really thinking too hard about anything else regarding the show.

00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:56.320
So the game is very bare bones in my opinion.

00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:58.540
And it comes off right away.

00:11:59.140 --> 00:12:05.260
Not because this is made by the same people, high-tech expressions, the guys who also made the Sesame Street games.

00:12:05.260 --> 00:12:10.980
So you immediately notice that there is no correct way to control which game you want to play.

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:15.680
No matter what button you hit, it just goes down and then up again in the menu like the Sesame Street games.

00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:19.020
That's not the problem, but it is like automatically a warning sign.

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:25.380
The real warning was as soon as you select which minigame you want to go into, you just immediately get dumped into it.

00:12:25.500 --> 00:12:32.800
Like it had already been going and now it's just like it's still happening while you're like just, okay, and now you take the wheel as Kermit.

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:35.420
Like, okay, like what do I do?

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:36.640
Like what am I supposed to be doing?

00:12:36.820 --> 00:12:40.400
And it turns out the thing you're supposed to be doing is exactly what it looks like.

00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:47.700
Not much. I kept going back and forth in my head as to whether like, I know that this is a kid's game.

00:12:48.020 --> 00:12:51.020
And I know that like this is not designed for me.

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:52.180
This is not for me.

00:12:52.300 --> 00:12:58.320
But like I kept going back and forth like, is this just a kid's game or is this actual shovelware?

00:12:58.620 --> 00:13:05.200
Yeah, I think I would lean towards shovelware because like we say this is a kid's game for something like Sesame Street.

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:10.360
And that's like, yeah, that's goal is to do something very different than like be a fun game.

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:12.200
This is trying to be a fun game.

00:13:12.340 --> 00:13:15.440
Even if it's for younger kids, it's trying to be a video game.

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:21.960
So like for it, you know, Mike, what you were just talking about, about it just throwing you into the levels.

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:30.820
I think the biggest, at least for me, the worst offender of this was the Kermit ones where sometimes I'm, I just, I'm starting on top of a rock that's damaging me.

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:36.780
There are times where the level spawns me on top of one of those logs that damages you and moves you.

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:40.840
And I just lose all my lives immediately before I get any agency as the player.

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:48.320
So like, I think that shows that it's like, this was not either not play tested or it was not polished enough.

00:13:48.320 --> 00:13:58.060
Yeah. Well, it's certainly, even if it is for kids, which I'm not going to challenge, like I agree that the difficulty is not really there other than that.

00:13:58.880 --> 00:14:02.520
I mean, there is a difficulty to it because of how long it goes on for.

00:14:02.740 --> 00:14:04.140
Yeah. But that's more in your head.

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:05.600
Yeah, exactly. It's in your head.

00:14:06.500 --> 00:14:14.000
The problem is, is that if it was for kids, they should take more time to like explain this, like how Sesame Street games do.

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:20.500
You know, the Sesame Street games might be guilty of holding your hand too much, but at least they are education games that are designed to do something.

00:14:20.660 --> 00:14:22.380
I get that these aren't education.

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:23.560
They're not teaching you anything.

00:14:23.560 --> 00:14:33.540
They just have a clear or maybe not so clear goal because you do kind of just feel like you're drifting endlessly in these levels until they suddenly tell you that they've been cleared.

00:14:33.900 --> 00:14:39.940
Yeah. But there's nothing really, like there's no setup.

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:45.480
Even the pig nap thing at the front of the thing, to Sean's point, these don't even feel like carnival games.

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:51.820
I get the idea that like Animal's supposed to maybe be in like a bumper cars ride or something.

00:14:52.100 --> 00:14:53.900
The bumper cars are the closest we got, yeah.

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:56.560
But it's not even like, it's not in a bumper cars environment.

00:14:56.560 --> 00:15:00.280
It would be better if you had to do like a survival against Dr.

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:03.100
Grump's henchmen in a bumper cars style game.

00:15:03.100 --> 00:15:05.420
We're like, oh, don't hit the side of the walls or something.

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:15.500
Instead, they just created these really long levels that auto scroll or you scroll depending on which level it is.

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:18.420
But like so if you're in the car, you control the speed.

00:15:18.420 --> 00:15:29.560
But if you're in the space shuttle or the Kermit the Frog rowing game, you know, like those games auto scroll.

00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:33.600
And so you're just kind of drifting and you think like, okay, is it multiple levels?

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:34.940
Like when does this end?

00:15:34.940 --> 00:15:37.300
And it goes on for a really long time.

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:41.780
I was at a point where I thought that like I was missing the point of the game.

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:47.880
Like I was supposed to have been doing something and this was just going to keep going on forever until I did that.

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:53.040
But no, I just had to wait for like eight or nine minutes.

00:15:53.740 --> 00:16:01.200
Yeah. And the issue for me with the go-kart one is that there's no incentive to go fast.

00:16:01.540 --> 00:16:03.500
Like there's no time limit.

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:09.480
It's not a race. There's a bunch of little obstacles that will hurt you and you have limited lives.

00:16:09.720 --> 00:16:14.540
So you can really just take your time and go really slow and make it really boring.

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:19.680
But like the only incentive to go fast is like because you're bored, you know.

00:16:19.900 --> 00:16:27.540
But like if you want to optimize, play this game optimally, like you should be just like inching along on this, which is so stupid.

00:16:27.980 --> 00:16:31.120
Like this is like the one time I would advocate for a time limit.

00:16:32.120 --> 00:16:38.420
Sure. I wonder if you just hugged the top or bottom of the screen and just tanked whatever damage.

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:41.160
Like could you just power right through it?

00:16:41.300 --> 00:16:43.820
I for some reason psychologically did not do that.

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:44.840
I did try that.

00:16:44.840 --> 00:16:48.200
I tried. It doesn't work because eventually you will.

00:16:48.200 --> 00:16:58.920
So I think it actually is designed to have you slowly drift like down on the screen so that you don't ever just stay in a perfect spot and slide through everything.

00:16:59.440 --> 00:17:06.460
And so then eventually you'll hit one of those like oil spills that will just cause you to spin out and then you'll be completely out of control.

00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:12.500
Let's talk about, we'll start with the car crash ones or car crash.

00:17:13.080 --> 00:17:14.220
That's what I was doing in it.

00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:19.020
Burnout. Same. But yeah, let's talk about the car level first since we're on that subject.

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:22.820
That's the one with the animal. You're dropped into this one.

00:17:22.820 --> 00:17:25.420
The car does move in eight directions.

00:17:26.180 --> 00:17:32.380
And while that sounds really intuitive for an NES game, it's kind of not helpful.

00:17:32.600 --> 00:17:34.400
It'd be better if it was a little more rigid.

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:40.820
There are things to like watch out for and things to collect, but it's mostly just obstacles.

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:48.020
The idea is just avoid everything and just keep moving on because you just want to get to the end as fast as possible.

00:17:48.020 --> 00:17:57.220
There's no real reward other than score, but it's kind of weird when there's score in a game that also has story because the score doesn't affect the story.

00:17:57.440 --> 00:18:05.100
So I still just advocate for like dodge everything because there's not even like cool power ups that like, oh, collect this thing and it'll make you go really fast.

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:09.500
Or this thing will launch you in the air so you don't have to worry about the obstacles on the ground.

00:18:09.600 --> 00:18:10.980
There's nothing like that in the game.

00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:14.440
So you basically just want to avoid everything and rush to the end of the stage.

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:19.880
Was there anything more to the game that I missed?

00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:24.040
Were there any like, oh, that's a clever obstacle to throw in this game?

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:26.440
That really took me for a spin.

00:18:27.100 --> 00:18:37.100
No, the one thing that there is that still doesn't make sense to me is a bunch of barrels that don't hurt you and don't seem to give you anything unless they're giving you points.

00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:40.220
And I wasn't noticing, but like you hit the barrel and it lifts up.

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:45.500
So I was convinced after a while that the key was going to be under one of these barrels and I had to find it.

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:48.220
But to my knowledge, those barrels are there for no reason.

00:18:48.820 --> 00:19:01.100
Yeah, I would say that my only note is like, it's sort of in the same vein that I don't think that like the legibility makes a lot of sense.

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:07.780
It almost seems like kind of reverse the kinds of things that you should be attracted to and the things that you want to avoid.

00:19:07.780 --> 00:19:13.520
Like you want to pick up what to me look like banana peels.

00:19:14.560 --> 00:19:21.940
And maybe you're not, maybe they're not banana peels, but with enough Mario Kart, I have been trained to avoid all banana peels.

00:19:21.940 --> 00:19:26.400
And I think that like, you don't even need that for it to look like a bad thing to hit.

00:19:26.880 --> 00:19:32.660
And then the thing you want to avoid, which I imagine are like cherry bombs, just look like cherries.

00:19:33.280 --> 00:19:42.380
And I think that cherries as a thing that you want to collect has existed for a while, even at this point in video games.

00:19:42.620 --> 00:19:44.080
So yeah, it was just odd.

00:19:44.260 --> 00:19:45.940
It was just a weird thing to do.

00:19:45.940 --> 00:19:50.080
And the things, I don't know if what you're talking about is the banana peels are these red flags.

00:19:50.400 --> 00:19:51.500
Are they flags?

00:19:51.960 --> 00:20:00.900
Yes. But even if you know that they're red flags, I think the term red flag is like definitively something you want to avoid, a red flag.

00:20:01.540 --> 00:20:04.280
That's true. There's also like greens, they are flags.

00:20:04.540 --> 00:20:06.060
I'm looking at it now, they're just freaking flags.

00:20:06.220 --> 00:20:07.400
But to me, they look like banana peels.

00:20:09.580 --> 00:20:10.580
You know what's funny too?

00:20:10.580 --> 00:20:18.100
If you just take it as Animal went off the bumper car's course, right?

00:20:18.180 --> 00:20:22.240
And now he's just riding around this car, which is something like Animal would do.

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:23.740
He's nuts, right?

00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:25.020
Now he's just riding it around.

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:27.480
This isn't like a course, you know?

00:20:27.560 --> 00:20:30.440
This isn't even like there's no clever turns or whatever.

00:20:30.440 --> 00:20:33.020
It's a straight line the whole way through.

00:20:33.320 --> 00:20:36.880
They couldn't even design like a racetrack for this.

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:40.560
Every single thing in this game is a straight line.

00:20:40.660 --> 00:20:44.380
There is no concept of turns in this game.

00:20:45.020 --> 00:20:48.000
You have to turn around the stuff that you don't want to hit.

00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:49.820
No, I know that.

00:20:49.940 --> 00:20:52.520
But you know what I mean? There's no turns on the course.

00:20:52.740 --> 00:20:54.040
Yeah, that bothers me.

00:20:54.320 --> 00:20:59.560
This would have been a good chance for a real racing segment instead of what we got.

00:20:59.560 --> 00:21:09.180
And while the key does eventually show up or whatever, it is possible to also just fly by that.

00:21:09.420 --> 00:21:11.620
Oh, I didn't even think that's a possibility.

00:21:11.860 --> 00:21:14.580
Yeah. Oh, it's worse in the auto-scroller.

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:28.540
So in the Kermit the Frog one, when you're in the rowboat, in that one, because it's an auto-scroll and because of the way – so the way that game works is you use the D-pad, use the left and the right to steer the boat.

00:21:28.540 --> 00:21:34.720
And then you either hold down to speed up or hold up to kind of like slow down the pace of the boat.

00:21:34.720 --> 00:21:43.740
But there's a very tight track with a lot of obstacles and a lot of things to avoid, very few things to pick up.

00:21:43.840 --> 00:21:51.200
But there is a reason to pick up things in this one because you're taking damage on everything you hit, so you do want to recover your health.

00:21:51.860 --> 00:21:58.640
If you miss the key at the end of this long adventure, it just resets you back to the beginning.

00:21:59.180 --> 00:22:01.760
You have to now play the entire stage again.

00:22:01.760 --> 00:22:08.660
Then, like, it just auto-scrolls you right back to the start, and now you have to do the whole thing again before you get a chance to collect the key.

00:22:08.900 --> 00:22:18.180
So I can't imagine how frustrating it would be to have, like, one health left but the key be placed in a spot where, like, you probably would take a hit to get across.

00:22:18.180 --> 00:22:23.420
Because there is very little in the sense of momentum on this.

00:22:23.420 --> 00:22:35.600
Like, you're either, like, in the correct spot and you're not going to take damage or you kind of have to just, like, you know, in certain platformers or action games we talk about sometimes you just want to take the damage hit to get the invincibility to move through it.

00:22:35.760 --> 00:22:40.460
That's kind of what happens in this river ride with Kermit as well.

00:22:40.460 --> 00:22:44.820
There's also some problems with, I think, like, just hitboxes too.

00:22:45.040 --> 00:22:55.380
I feel like I have this complaint in most games, but especially in a game like this where there isn't really much else to do aside from avoid things,

00:22:55.380 --> 00:23:02.400
you would think that maybe having hitboxes that were tight to the actual sprite would be important.

00:23:02.400 --> 00:23:07.380
Yeah, or hitboxes and also, like, detection of hits.

00:23:07.880 --> 00:23:09.980
Or not even detection, but, like, feedback.

00:23:10.580 --> 00:23:13.720
Because, like, if you run into a rock, it's just, like, health draining.

00:23:14.320 --> 00:23:15.520
There's no, like... Just melt you.

00:23:15.560 --> 00:23:17.320
There's no, like, you don't get pushed back or anything.

00:23:17.960 --> 00:23:22.380
Sometimes you can get stuck on a rock and just watch your health drain and, like, you can't move.

00:23:22.940 --> 00:23:24.600
So it just feels really weird.

00:23:53.040 --> 00:23:57.920
The next ride, Gonzo's space ride.

00:23:57.920 --> 00:24:08.200
Asteroid. That's probably the closest we get to anything other, any other video game we've played where, like, you can make the case that this is, you know, asteroids or something, I suppose.

00:24:08.820 --> 00:24:12.500
It is an auto-scroll shooter, so in some ways it's even a shmup.

00:24:14.040 --> 00:24:16.300
But it's barely any of that.

00:24:16.460 --> 00:24:18.860
You do, you are, you're in the spaceship.

00:24:18.880 --> 00:24:21.640
You can control again in the eight directions.

00:24:22.000 --> 00:24:33.380
But this one with the thrust, so that's what reminds me of Asteroid, where, like, you have this momentum that powers through and you kind of have to, if you're going too fast in one direction, you gotta turn the ship around and thrust in the other direction.

00:24:33.380 --> 00:24:47.260
So there is a game here, and the slow scroll in this one isn't as painful because I feel like it is necessary, especially if we're arguing that this game is somewhat for kids.

00:24:48.040 --> 00:24:57.560
That it gives younger players the chance to choose which path they want to go in because there are sometimes branching paths with different, and branching paths is being polite.

00:24:57.760 --> 00:25:00.820
It's just, you know, oh, we're going to put a bar in the middle of the screen.

00:25:00.820 --> 00:25:01.960
I mean, yeah, do you want to go up or down?

00:25:02.660 --> 00:25:04.440
But there are things in here, too.

00:25:04.540 --> 00:25:05.680
There are other enemies.

00:25:05.920 --> 00:25:07.520
There are drifting rocks.

00:25:07.740 --> 00:25:11.880
There are fuel canisters.

00:25:12.660 --> 00:25:15.580
Yeah, sure. The meatballs were the rocks, in my opinion.

00:25:19.560 --> 00:25:24.060
But at the end of the auto-scroll, this one doesn't have, like, a key you can miss.

00:25:24.060 --> 00:25:29.880
It does have a boss fight, I guess you can call it, where you do shoot at an enemy spaceship.

00:25:29.880 --> 00:25:32.280
And then you're rewarded with the key.

00:25:32.720 --> 00:25:34.120
It poops out the key.

00:25:34.980 --> 00:25:36.500
Very, very well said.

00:25:37.220 --> 00:25:42.080
Yeah. All that to say, like, this one actually felt like they might have been onto something.

00:25:42.420 --> 00:25:45.460
Like, if they just did this with the other Muppet games, it would have been okay.

00:25:45.980 --> 00:25:48.020
It's definitely the best one.

00:25:49.040 --> 00:25:52.720
I think that there's still a little bit of, like, wait, what am I doing?

00:25:52.840 --> 00:25:54.380
Like, this still needs a little bit of a setup.

00:25:54.380 --> 00:25:57.320
But yeah, I mean, this is definitely the most...

00:25:57.320 --> 00:26:01.500
It is the most, like, the execution was the best here.

00:26:02.080 --> 00:26:10.980
But it's a pretty low bar of just like, okay, at least it feels like Asteroids is the best we can do so far.

00:26:10.980 --> 00:26:18.060
And then the last game of the four minigames with Fozzie Bear here, which first off, nobody likes Fozzie, right?

00:26:18.380 --> 00:26:20.200
I thought he was cool.

00:26:20.620 --> 00:26:21.420
I thought he was beloved.

00:26:22.000 --> 00:26:23.040
Oh, Waka Waka?

00:26:25.060 --> 00:26:28.040
Yeah. Oh, now that you say that, I love him.

00:26:28.320 --> 00:26:29.880
Right, yeah. Now you know who he is.

00:26:30.540 --> 00:26:33.720
Fozzie Bear. Amaze is a carnival thing.

00:26:33.840 --> 00:26:34.780
I think we can agree on that.

00:26:34.780 --> 00:26:37.000
This is the one that takes place inside the carnival.

00:26:37.000 --> 00:26:40.040
Maybe the other ones took place in, like, the parking lot.

00:26:41.140 --> 00:26:43.340
You know, like, he wrote the...

00:26:43.340 --> 00:26:46.120
I will grant that mazes exist in carnivals.

00:26:46.420 --> 00:26:47.260
He wrote the...

00:26:47.260 --> 00:26:49.420
Mazes where the walls are ice cream sundaes.

00:26:49.860 --> 00:26:51.520
But that, like, they are.

00:26:51.740 --> 00:26:54.160
And it's just like, what could they have done?

00:26:54.300 --> 00:26:58.960
Like, they could have used literally anything to make these walls.

00:26:58.960 --> 00:27:12.600
And in order to make the walls look like, like, have any sense of, like, oh, I can walk here but not walk there, they chose something that just sort of looks like a, like a MS paintbrush.

00:27:13.400 --> 00:27:14.860
Yeah. I don't know.

00:27:15.220 --> 00:27:16.560
Yeah, like a stamp tool.

00:27:16.740 --> 00:27:23.540
It's very, it's very hard to read the maze with this, like, this pattern that they're using.

00:27:23.900 --> 00:27:34.080
And the loop of this is very strange, too, where, like, you have to collect three prizes and then they just kind of, like, spawn.

00:27:34.120 --> 00:27:37.380
So you just collect it and then you collect the next one and then you collect the next one.

00:27:37.500 --> 00:27:40.660
Like, you don't see them. It's barely a maze in that sense.

00:27:40.780 --> 00:27:41.980
Like, I thought it was going to be this.

00:27:42.480 --> 00:27:44.820
I just thought you were going to see this thing.

00:27:46.060 --> 00:27:49.140
That is actually a Fozzie Bear-style joke, Sean.

00:27:49.240 --> 00:27:50.200
I don't know if you know that.

00:27:50.200 --> 00:27:53.760
You made it. Yeah, but you connected it.

00:27:55.000 --> 00:27:58.420
Also, real quick, is he being chased by, like, a mini Fozzie Bear?

00:27:59.160 --> 00:28:02.000
No, there's a mouse Muppet, too, and I forget his name.

00:28:02.100 --> 00:28:03.640
Oh, okay. A little mouse.

00:28:04.040 --> 00:28:05.440
Oh, yeah, Rizzo.

00:28:05.500 --> 00:28:06.840
Rizzo the rat. Oh, okay.

00:28:07.620 --> 00:28:08.900
He's not a mouse, he's a rat.

00:28:09.360 --> 00:28:11.160
My bad. Sorry, Riz.

00:28:12.820 --> 00:28:14.080
But you know what I mean?

00:28:14.100 --> 00:28:16.440
Like, it's kind of weird that these things just, like, spawn in.

00:28:16.440 --> 00:28:21.240
Like, they're not purposefully placed, and then it's only after you, like, you collect

00:28:21.240 --> 00:28:24.200
one, and then the other one doesn't, like, pop up right away.

00:28:24.720 --> 00:28:28.500
It sometimes takes some time for it to be like, all right, fine, we'll throw this one,

00:28:28.500 --> 00:28:29.920
I don't know, over here.

00:28:30.060 --> 00:28:31.240
And they just go there.

00:28:31.660 --> 00:28:34.360
But, again, it's not really a maze.

00:28:34.480 --> 00:28:38.680
You see the entire, a maze is where you don't know where you're going.

00:28:38.720 --> 00:28:43.960
Yeah, yeah. This would be like if the entirety of Metroid was on one screen, you know?

00:28:44.180 --> 00:28:45.760
What would you call this, then?

00:28:46.060 --> 00:28:48.240
This is like a walk in the park with Fozzie Bear.

00:28:48.440 --> 00:28:50.300
A walk in the park with Fozzie Bear.

00:28:50.300 --> 00:28:51.540
It's like a path. Yeah.

00:28:52.220 --> 00:28:55.240
And if that really is Rizzo the rat, he's not a bad guy.

00:28:56.060 --> 00:28:59.060
So he's not, like, in the show.

00:28:59.420 --> 00:29:00.960
He's not a villain. He's like Gonzo's friend.

00:29:01.400 --> 00:29:03.340
Oh, okay. Well, do people like Gonzo?

00:29:03.940 --> 00:29:05.260
Gonzo's my favorite Muppet.

00:29:05.680 --> 00:29:06.960
Oh, okay. I don't know.

00:29:07.080 --> 00:29:09.220
Nobody asked me earlier, so I thought I'd just say that right.

00:29:09.320 --> 00:29:13.980
He always struck me as someone, like, that didn't, like, he wasn't really considered

00:29:13.980 --> 00:29:16.720
part of the clique. That's why he's my favorite.

00:29:17.120 --> 00:29:22.560
Oh, okay. But I just wanted to, you know, once again, you just have to do this.

00:29:22.660 --> 00:29:27.140
There's nothing that indicates that you might be, like, halfway through or, like, near the

00:29:27.140 --> 00:29:31.960
end. It all just sort of ends after, like, doing this for eight to ten minutes.

00:29:32.180 --> 00:29:37.380
Right. Screen one of 20 would have been nice to see, you know, as you're progressing along.

00:29:37.380 --> 00:29:39.220
Like, how many more times do I got to do this?

00:29:39.320 --> 00:29:43.480
Yeah. Are there two Rizzo's?

00:29:43.640 --> 00:29:44.860
Because there's two Rizzo's in this game.

00:29:45.280 --> 00:29:46.880
There are not two Rizzo's.

00:29:47.520 --> 00:29:51.940
Good. I don't know if, like, Rizzo has cousins.

00:29:52.800 --> 00:29:53.920
Yeah. You know?

00:29:54.360 --> 00:29:58.980
Plankton has, like, a million cousins, so maybe that's the same situation with Rizzo the

00:29:58.980 --> 00:29:59.980
rat. Maybe.

00:30:00.820 --> 00:30:04.400
Plankton, famously not a Muppet, shouldn't have been mentioned in this episode, but.

00:30:05.740 --> 00:30:12.720
Well, we all kind of agreed that the Gonzo space level was the best level.

00:30:12.840 --> 00:30:14.100
Do we agree that this is the worst level?

00:30:14.780 --> 00:30:16.360
This is barely a video game.

00:30:16.420 --> 00:30:18.600
I don't know. Yeah. There's nothing fun about it.

00:30:18.760 --> 00:30:21.340
You're just walking slowly around, picking things up.

00:30:21.560 --> 00:30:22.460
I was going to say.

00:30:22.780 --> 00:30:23.860
And I've never. Go ahead.

00:30:23.900 --> 00:30:29.480
I've never seen a video game get walking in four directions wrong.

00:30:30.060 --> 00:30:31.600
But, like, it doesn't work.

00:30:31.860 --> 00:30:35.900
Sometimes I hit left and I'm, like, too close to something and it just takes me down or right.

00:30:36.200 --> 00:30:38.460
Like, I don't know how that can happen.

00:30:38.680 --> 00:30:40.160
It's using the menu logic.

00:30:40.660 --> 00:30:44.860
Yeah. Any button just takes you the next direction.

00:30:45.120 --> 00:30:46.100
The next direction.

00:30:46.280 --> 00:30:52.100
Yeah. And you could argue that, again, they're going for reference to a classic arcade game here

00:30:52.100 --> 00:30:56.000
with Pac-Man, but they didn't do anything like that.

00:30:56.340 --> 00:30:59.020
The Rizzo the rats don't act like ghosts.

00:30:59.480 --> 00:31:03.960
There's no, like, there's no, like, oh, collect every pellet on the screen or whatever.

00:31:04.120 --> 00:31:07.060
Collect these randomly spawning accessories.

00:31:07.700 --> 00:31:09.880
It's like bow ties and gift boxes, right?

00:31:10.560 --> 00:31:14.300
Yeah. Collect these things, which you were never told to collect, by the way, either.

00:31:14.500 --> 00:31:19.380
So it's never communicated that you have to collect these three things for the stage to end.

00:31:19.520 --> 00:31:21.920
It just happens to end after you collect those three things.

00:31:21.920 --> 00:31:24.460
And then you just say, well, I guess I'll do that again the next stage, right?

00:31:24.560 --> 00:31:30.700
For all you know, just to the point of the length of all these games, there's something else you're supposed to be doing

00:31:30.700 --> 00:31:33.860
