But that held my interest for a little bit longer than this game normally would have.

01:02:24.900 --> 01:02:35.240
It's definitely like becomes like a big slap fight because of how I guess how like rapid you can just like swing your sword.

01:02:35.400 --> 01:02:39.700
There's no cool down. There's no there's no like kickback from the enemies or anything.

01:02:39.700 --> 01:02:43.640
So you kind of just like both sitting there holding your shields up like rock and suck.

01:02:43.960 --> 01:02:44.860
Slapping each other with your swords.

01:02:45.180 --> 01:02:54.400
Exactly. Yeah. And as soon as someone lets an opening, lets their shield down for a second, like you can very quickly drain your opponent's health by just like mashing away on their weakness.

01:02:54.400 --> 01:03:10.080
I remember we did make a big deal about the Trojan multiplayer on the episode because it was like pre Street Fighter, you know, combat and that that idea of just one V one on a screen.

01:03:10.080 --> 01:03:16.160
But the actual game, too, I was I definitely gave it a play it like I really liked the game.

01:03:16.280 --> 01:03:19.440
And from what I remember, the boss fights were pretty good, too.

01:03:20.260 --> 01:03:21.560
It's it's Capcom.

01:03:21.560 --> 01:03:25.980
So I trust that it's still OK, but I haven't revisited it.

01:03:26.140 --> 01:03:30.380
Maybe I should. Yeah, I think it has like both very satisfying.

01:03:30.580 --> 01:03:38.880
Like the same thing that makes it sometimes feel a little jank to me is like that lack of feedback also makes it very satisfying.

01:03:38.880 --> 01:03:44.560
Because I do feel like I could just kind of like run through and just like slice away at enemies and I mow them down very easily.

01:03:46.000 --> 01:03:49.760
And there is a satisfaction element, too, with the shield.

01:03:49.760 --> 01:03:59.900
Like once you kind of get the timing down with your shield, being able to utilize a block button like this, it's weird that it's not more common.

01:04:00.100 --> 01:04:04.100
Like I know like Legend of Zelda has a shield, but it's not like it's not used in the same way.

01:04:04.220 --> 01:04:06.780
It kind of just has more to do with like which way you're facing kind of thing.

01:04:06.780 --> 01:04:11.320
But this felt very it felt very good to to be able to defend yourself in that way.

01:04:11.440 --> 01:04:14.980
You could even kind of crouch and defend and make yourself like a very small target.

01:04:15.320 --> 01:04:25.620
And not to say that you're invincible in that way, but it does feel like you have to use different strategy a little bit of like, do I want to be more mobile?

01:04:25.840 --> 01:04:28.760
Do I want to kind of sit here and tank hits?

01:04:29.460 --> 01:04:31.580
But yeah, it feels it feels good to play.

01:04:31.680 --> 01:04:38.860
I don't know if I would give it a play it now after having played a bunch of other things, but like I'm teetering on the edge of that.

01:04:39.220 --> 01:04:40.860
Definitely not wouldn't say it's essential.

01:04:41.080 --> 01:04:54.020
I just remember to Trojan was our first episode of season three, 1987, and it feels graphically like a leap from what we had been seeing in 85 and 86.

01:04:54.920 --> 01:05:03.620
It had more promise of like, oh, you can push this system more and games can look different than the black box games.

01:05:04.320 --> 01:05:05.680
Yeah. All right.

01:05:05.940 --> 01:05:10.780
What else? The third and final one and my favorite of the three was Breakthrough.

01:05:12.340 --> 01:05:13.820
I don't know if you guys remember Breakthrough.

01:05:13.980 --> 01:05:18.100
I was assuming Breakthrough was going to be like an Arkanoid type thing.

01:05:18.380 --> 01:05:19.840
Oh, yeah, yeah. It is very much not.

01:05:20.300 --> 01:05:28.380
But yeah, so this one I do actually have visual memories of.

01:05:29.400 --> 01:05:32.640
Unlike. Yeah, I feel like it sticks out a little bit, right?

01:05:32.660 --> 01:05:34.520
Yeah. Like it's a it's different.

01:05:34.760 --> 01:05:43.880
It looks nice. And at first I was a little like, OK, this is going to be just like a really janky just based on like the the not the menu screen,

01:05:43.880 --> 01:05:53.620
but the like level intro screen, which looks literally like a like blank VCR screen, you know, that like blue screen at the play button up there.

01:05:53.940 --> 01:06:00.440
Yeah. But as I started playing it like this one, I really kind of got into this is the game.

01:06:00.520 --> 01:06:08.920
If any if anyone listening doesn't remember, this is a game you're driving a car through like a war, I guess.

01:06:09.280 --> 01:06:15.960
And you're trying to, you know, basically you're just trying to get through all these defenses, all these enemy defenses.

01:06:15.960 --> 01:06:18.140
But you control your speed.

01:06:18.180 --> 01:06:22.220
So it's not like it's not like exactly an auto scroller.

01:06:22.320 --> 01:06:23.640
I mean, it is technically auto scrolling.

01:06:24.000 --> 01:06:29.720
But and you have to avoid obstacles, shoot down enemies and you do die a lot.

01:06:29.800 --> 01:06:32.100
Like it's like one of those games where there's like a lot coming at you.

01:06:32.320 --> 01:06:41.680
But I think what makes this game for me so playable and so much more enjoyable than other games like this is that you basically have unlimited continues.

01:06:42.740 --> 01:06:46.400
Not that that's always a good thing, but I think in this case, it's like this.

01:06:46.520 --> 01:06:54.800
This almost gave me like the kind of satisfaction I get with Cuphead or, you know, or even Mike and I recently Mike recently showed me Super Monkey Ball.

01:06:55.200 --> 01:07:06.520
Where like and I've never played that before, but like we're like, hey, if I could just keep playing this level over and over again, like because I'm running into this challenge, like I'm fine with progressing slowly in that way.

01:07:06.520 --> 01:07:11.280
Because there are a lot of obstacles in this game where I get or it's like, OK, I keep dying, keep dying.

01:07:11.380 --> 01:07:17.480
I can feel myself getting a little better at it because I have I have unlimited times that I can try it again.

01:07:17.820 --> 01:07:21.220
So I only got to like the third level in this, but there's like five levels.

01:07:21.580 --> 01:07:24.240
But it took a long time to do that.

01:07:24.400 --> 01:07:32.440
It took a long time to do that, but it didn't feel like I had to memorize so much because I didn't have to start back at the beginning after every like six deaths or something.

01:07:33.220 --> 01:07:40.140
Wasn't this the game, too, that actually had like a story reason for why you're apparently like this one guy going to war alone?

01:07:40.360 --> 01:07:45.900
Like it was like you were tasked with like just sort of like scouting ahead or something like that.

01:07:46.440 --> 01:07:51.080
I didn't read the manual, but I did listen to the original episode.

01:07:51.620 --> 01:07:58.820
And you guys sort of talked about that a little bit about like and I think, Sean, you said something like that.

01:07:58.820 --> 01:08:06.760
The only way that this could happen is if like the other military was having like a military wide field day and it was just like a free day for them.

01:08:06.880 --> 01:08:10.460
And then you came driving in and then they're like, oh, shit, there's an enemy here.

01:08:10.660 --> 01:08:11.960
That's something I'd say.

01:08:12.180 --> 01:08:19.920
Yeah. Joe, I can't remember, but the breakthrough also has your car can jump in the air.

01:08:20.520 --> 01:08:22.640
Yes. And you're go ahead.

01:08:22.740 --> 01:08:30.880
Sorry. I was going to say and I remember that there are certain moments in the game where you have to jump because otherwise you will fall into a pitfall.

01:08:30.880 --> 01:08:41.140
But that maybe a complaint was that like sometimes you don't know how long, like how high you have to jump and how long those pitfalls are.

01:08:41.600 --> 01:08:43.320
Is that is that a problem in this game?

01:08:43.420 --> 01:08:49.480
I think I had that complaint at first where I would there would be it wasn't a pitfall.

01:08:49.480 --> 01:08:51.100
The first one, it was like a landslide.

01:08:51.240 --> 01:08:55.640
I was trying to jump over and I would always not be at the right speed to get enough distance.

01:08:56.460 --> 01:09:00.080
But then I realized I kind of did get the feel of that, first of all.

01:09:00.180 --> 01:09:08.440
And I also realized that like you really have to decide where you're going to jump, like, you know, like which part of the landslide you had to jump over and you got to jump over the narrow end.

01:09:08.860 --> 01:09:17.660
I mean, you can jump over the long end, but you have to be going full speed, which is admittedly tough on the first time you run across that obstacle because you don't know it's there.

01:09:17.820 --> 01:09:21.440
And sometimes you don't have enough time to get up to speed to make the jump.

01:09:21.500 --> 01:09:22.820
But that was just the first one later.

01:09:22.820 --> 01:09:26.660
The second level has like bridges that have broken areas and you do have to make jumps like that.

01:09:26.760 --> 01:09:32.980
But I feel like by then I had gotten the hang of it where like I was dying much more from enemies than from falling.

01:09:33.400 --> 01:09:36.880
I'm glad you replayed these games or played them for the first time.

01:09:37.020 --> 01:09:38.500
I'm glad we got a chance to talk about them again.

